\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Bifurcation angle on a made-up left main bifurcation, computed with the thesis code. Along the LAD and the LCx, points are placed every 0.5\,mm between 5 and 10\,mm from the bifurcation point $O$, measured along the centerline. A line fitted through each set of points, dashed back towards $O$, gives the direction $\mathbf  {u}_{\mathrm  {LAD}}$ or $\mathbf  {u}_{\mathrm  {LCx}}$ in which the artery leaves the bifurcation, and $\theta $ is the angle between the two directions.\relax }}{29}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method-angle}{{6.1}{29}{Bifurcation angle on a made-up left main bifurcation, computed with the thesis code. Along the LAD and the LCx, points are placed every 0.5\,mm between 5 and 10\,mm from the bifurcation point $O$, measured along the centerline. A line fitted through each set of points, dashed back towards $O$, gives the direction $\mathbf {u}_{\mathrm {LAD}}$ or $\mathbf {u}_{\mathrm {LCx}}$ in which the artery leaves the bifurcation, and $\theta $ is the angle between the two directions.\relax }{figure.caption.18}{}}
