\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces Curvature along a made-up centerline, computed with the thesis code. At a point $P_i$ on each bend, the points $B_i$ and $F_i$ lie 5\,mm in a straight line behind and ahead of it, and $\kappa _i$ is the inverse of the radius of the circle through the three points. The tighter the bend, the smaller the circle and the larger $\kappa $, while on a straight stretch the three points lie on a line and $\kappa = 0$.\relax }}{32}{figure.caption.20}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method-curvature-radius}{{6.3}{32}{Curvature along a made-up centerline, computed with the thesis code. At a point $P_i$ on each bend, the points $B_i$ and $F_i$ lie 5\,mm in a straight line behind and ahead of it, and $\kappa _i$ is the inverse of the radius of the circle through the three points. The tighter the bend, the smaller the circle and the larger $\kappa $, while on a straight stretch the three points lie on a line and $\kappa = 0$.\relax }{figure.caption.20}{}}
\newlabel{fig:method-curvature-radius@cref}{{[figure][3][6]6.3}{[1][31][]32}}
